<script id="landing-structured-data" type="application/ld+json">
  <%= Phoenix.HTML.raw(Jason.encode!(@structured_data)) %>
</script>

<div class="min-h-full">
  <header class="measure flex items-center justify-between gap-6 px-6 py-5">
    <Layouts.logo class="text-[15px]" />
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-xs">
      <nav
        id="landing-nav"
        aria-label="Landing page"
        class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2"
      >
        <a href="#what-it-does" class="act">What it does</a>
        <a href="#run-it-yourself" class="act">Run it yourself</a>
        <a href="#comparison" class="act">Compare</a>
        <a href="#faq" class="act">FAQ</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ashishbishnoi18/superx" class="act">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
        <Layouts.theme_toggle />
        <.link :if={@x_configured} id="landing-sign-in" href={~p"/auth/x"} class="act-key">
          Sign in with 𝕏
        </.link>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="measure px-6">
    <section class="py-20 sm:py-28" aria-labelledby="landing-title">
      <p class="nb-eyebrow mb-6">Free · open source · self-hosted</p>

      <h1
        id="landing-title"
        class="max-w-[18ch] text-[clamp(2.25rem,6vw,3.75rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.035em]"
      >
        Grow on 𝕏 without living on 𝕏
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[58ch] text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
        SuperX is a free, open-source, self-hosted X (Twitter) scheduler and growth tool.
        Draft and review posts, keep a publishing queue, work through replies, and track
        results from one application you run yourself.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[58ch] leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
        It is an open-source alternative to superx.so. The <a
          href="https://github.com/ashishbishnoi18/superx"
          class="act underline underline-offset-4"
        >
          source is published on GitHub</a>, while the application and Postgres database run on
        infrastructure you control.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-9">
        <.link
          :if={@x_configured}
          id="hero-sign-in"
          href={~p"/auth/x"}
          class="act-key text-[15px]"
        >
          Sign in with 𝕏 →
        </.link>

        <p
          :if={!@x_configured}
          id="x-configuration-help"
          class="max-w-[52ch] text-muted-foreground"
        >
          <span class="nb-mono text-[11px] text-destructive">not configured</span>
          <br /> X sign-in isn't configured yet. Set
          <code class="nb-mono text-[12px] text-foreground">X_CLIENT_ID</code>
          and <code class="nb-mono text-[12px] text-foreground">X_CLIENT_SECRET</code>,
          then restart. The repository lists every variable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="what-it-does" class="flex flex-col pb-24" aria-labelledby="what-it-does-title">
      <header class="pb-8">
        <p class="nb-eyebrow mb-3">What it does</p>
        <h2
          id="what-it-does-title"
          class="text-[1.75rem] font-semibold leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.03em]"
        >
          A practical workflow for showing up consistently
        </h2>
      </header>

      <div
        :for={{feature, index} <- Enum.with_index(@features, 1)}
        class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-7 border-t border-border py-7 last:border-b sm:grid-cols-[7.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"
      >
        <span class="nb-mono text-[11px] text-faint">
          {String.pad_leading(to_string(index), 2, "0")}
        </span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">{feature.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1.5 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">{feature.body}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="run-it-yourself"
      class="border-t border-border py-20"
      aria-labelledby="run-it-yourself-title"
    >
      <p class="nb-eyebrow mb-3">Run it yourself</p>
      <h2
        id="run-it-yourself-title"
        class="text-[1.75rem] font-semibold leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.03em]"
      >
        Deploy the app and Postgres with Docker Compose
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
        Start from a clone of the GitHub repository. You need Docker, a domain, two generated
        application secrets, and X OAuth credentials. Copy the environment template, fill in
        its required values, then run:
      </p>
      <pre
        id="self-host-commands"
        class="nb-mono mt-7 overflow-x-auto border-y border-border py-5 text-[12px] leading-[1.8] text-foreground"
      ><code phx-no-curly-interpolation>git clone https://github.com/ashishbishnoi18/superx.git
cd superx
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up -d --build
docker compose exec app /app/bin/migrate</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] text-[12px] leading-[1.6] text-faint">
        The environment template names every required and optional key. Back up the database,
        uploads volume, and <code class="nb-mono text-[11px] text-foreground">SUPERX_VAULT_KEY</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      id="comparison"
      class="border-t border-border py-20"
      aria-labelledby="comparison-title"
    >
      <p class="nb-eyebrow mb-3">Honest comparison</p>
      <h2
        id="comparison-title"
        class="text-[1.75rem] font-semibold leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.03em]"
      >
        Self-hosted control costs operator time
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
        SuperX suits people who value source access and data control more than a managed setup.
        A hosted tool is the better trade when you do not want to operate the software or manage
        separate provider accounts.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto">
        <table id="hosted-comparison" class="w-full min-w-[42rem] border-collapse text-left">
          <caption class="sr-only">
            Self-hosted SuperX compared with hosted X growth tools
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-y border-border">
              <th scope="col" class="nb-mono py-4 pr-6 text-[11px] font-medium text-faint">
                Trade-off
              </th>
              <th scope="col" class="nb-mono py-4 pr-6 text-[11px] font-medium text-faint">
                Self-hosted SuperX
              </th>
              <th scope="col" class="nb-mono py-4 text-[11px] font-medium text-faint">
                Hosted alternative
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="py-5 pr-6 text-[13px] font-semibold">Cost</th>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 pr-6 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                No SuperX subscription; you pay for your server and provider usage.
              </td>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                A recurring plan usually bundles the application and its operation.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="py-5 pr-6 text-[13px] font-semibold">Data</th>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 pr-6 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                Records live in your Postgres database; configured integrations receive data when called.
              </td>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                The vendor hosts application data and chooses its integration boundaries.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="py-5 pr-6 text-[13px] font-semibold">Operations</th>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 pr-6 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                You deploy, upgrade, monitor, rotate secrets, and restore backups.
              </td>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                The vendor handles uptime, updates, backups, and support.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="py-5 pr-6 text-[13px] font-semibold">Public X data</th>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 pr-6 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                Discovery, feeds, mentions, and Signals need a data source you configure and fund.
              </td>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                A hosted product may include an established corpus and managed data access.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="py-5 pr-6 text-[13px] font-semibold">Control</th>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 pr-6 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                Inspect and change the source, database, limits, and deployment.
              </td>
              <td class="max-w-[30ch] py-5 leading-[1.6] text-muted-foreground">
                Faster onboarding, but behavior and roadmap remain with the vendor.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="faq" class="border-t border-border py-20" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <p class="nb-eyebrow mb-3">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="text-[1.75rem] font-semibold leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.03em]">
        What self-hosting actually involves
      </h2>

      <div id="faq-list" class="mt-8">
        <article :for={faq <- @faqs} class="border-t border-border py-7 last:border-b">
          <h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">{faq.question}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-[72ch] leading-[1.7] text-muted-foreground">{faq.answer}</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-border py-7">
    <div class="measure flex flex-col gap-1 px-6 text-[12px] text-faint sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
      <p>SuperX — free, open-source, self-hosted X growth software</p>
      <nav aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#landing-nav" class="act">Back to top ↑</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </footer>
</div>
